sarah-sales: Heads-up: Acme onboarding POC tomorrow 11am PST. They want streaming + tool/function calls + strict structured JSON outputs. Need quick alignment on SDK examples, SSO/KMS requirements, and a two-slide cost comparison (Hosted vs Dedicated vs Private). Who can take the runbook?

devon-eng: I can. Do we know auth method? SAML for SSO or short-lived creds? Also want to confirm if their middleware supports multiplex websockets.

sarah-sales: They want SAML SSO to their IdP for enterprise auth. They also require customer-managed KMS for at-rest model artifacts and logs. Their infra team prefers Dedicated for steady QPS but wants pricing options.

jen-solutions: Sharing a tiny runnable JS SDK streaming + tool call example for them to try locally (minimal):

jen-solutions: ```js
import Redwood from '@redwood/inference';
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.RW_API_KEY });
const stream = client.streaming.generate({
  model: 'gpt-redwood-2',
  input: 'Extract invoices as JSON',
  streaming: true,
  tool_calls: true,
});
for await (const chunk of stream) {
  if (chunk.type === 'tool_call') {
    console.log('TOOL CALL', chunk.name, chunk.args);
  } else if (chunk.type === 'delta') {
    process.stdout.write(chunk.text);
  }
}
```

lia-ml: For structured outputs, recommend `output_schema` + a lightweight validator on the client. We'll drop a prompt-set that exercises edge cases (missing fields, extra arrays).

devon-eng: About multiplexing: their middleware expects one WS per user. Our SDK supports multiplexing but we can provide a Node proxy to convert single-conn clients into multiplexed streams. I'll attach a gist. ETA 4pm.

jen-solutions: Also sharing a small Docker demo wrapper if they prefer running isolated examples for security review.

sec-team: @sarah-sales capture these security asks in the questionnaire: data residency (EU/US), BYOK KMS support, SOC2 + pen test reports, network diagram, logs retention policy, and DPA. Also confirm signed callback flow for function/tool calls and mTLS for internal webhook endpoints.

sarah-sales: Noted. I'll send the questionnaire and loop in legal for DPA.

lia-ml: For POC function calls: we support a `signed_callback_url` metadata field so model-triggered tool calls can POST to a short-lived signed URL. Recommend TTL <= 60s and HMAC signature in query + mTLS. Example payload we use in streaming events:

jen-solutions: ```json
{
  "type": "tool_call",
  "name": "lookup_invoice",
  "args": { "invoice_id": "INV-123" },
  "signed_callback_url": "https://acme.internal/cb?sig=...&exp=..."
}
```

devon-eng: Security note: recommend mutual TLS + IP allowlist on their webhook. We'll provide cert examples and a short-run CA setup doc.

lia-ml: Pricing ballpark for 10M tokens/month: hosted generation naive calc is expensive at scale. Quick committed Dedicated range estimate: $6k - $12k/month depending on model variant and quantization choices. I'll produce a two-slide cost breakdown (Hosted vs Dedicated vs Private) and model suggestions by EOD.

jen-solutions: For the SDK snippet, I'll also include a schema-assert/validation example and a tiny replay test for edge-case outputs. ETA 3pm.

devon-eng: I'll draft the Dedicated architecture diagram showing request flow, where the KMS sits (customer VPC), and the handshake for SAML + SCIM provisioning. ETA EOD draft.

sec-team: Also clarify logs retention options: Hosted default 30d, Dedicated configurable up to 365d for an additional fee, Private controlled by customer. I'll add this to the security answers doc.

sarah-sales: Action items / owners: 
- devon-eng: proxy gist + Node example + arch diagram draft (ETA 4pm / EOD)
- jen-solutions: runnable SDK snippets + structured-output prompt set + Docker demo (ETA 3pm)
- lia-ml: Dedicated pricing calc & model recommendations + prompt set suggestions (ETA EOD)
- sec-team: security checklist answers + required docs list (ETA EOD)

sarah-sales: Demo scheduled 11:00 PST tomorrow. Please join the call. I'll send invites now. :thumbsup:

